ate limiting on API endpoints. Exporters (CSV/JSON) and list endpoints are vulnerable to abuse or resource exhaustion attacks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"app/api/_lib/respond.ts\",\n      \"line\": 28,\n      \"description\": \"No request size limit enforcement. Malicious clients could send extremely large JSON bodies causing memory exhaustion or DoS.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"app/api/runs/route.ts, app/api/conflicts/route.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"description\": \"No request timeout configuration visible. Long-running database queries could accumulate and deplete connection pool.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"lib/audit-detail.ts\",\n      \"line\": 40,\n      \"description\": \"Audit detail data from database rendered without explicit type-narrowing in all consumers. While Zod validation prevents injection at API boundaries, the detail field is open JSONB—downstream rendering (not shown) must properly escape output.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 72,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"Implement resource-level authorization (RBAC/ABAC) to verify users can only access runs/conflicts/audit logs they're entitled to. Add a checks like: `const authorizedRuns = await getUserRuns(reviewerId); if (!authorizedRuns.has(runId)) return notFound();`\",\n    \"Redact schema information from validation error responses. Return generic errors to clients: `{ error: 'Invalid request body.' }` and log detailed issues server-side only.\",\n    \"Add explicit CSRF token validation to all state-changing endpoints. Integrate `csrf` middleware and validate `x-csrf-token` headers on POST/PATCH/DELETE.\",\n    \"Implement rate limiting on all API endpoints. Use a rate-limit middleware (e.g., `next-rate-limit`) with per-IP or per-user quotas. Export endpoints should have strict limits (e.g., 5 requests/minute).\",\n    \"Add request size limits via middleware. Set `